{
  "_about": [
    "How a fleet is ranked and counted, once, for every side that does it (ov-166).",
    "The relay composes the lock screen card (composeFleet in services/relay/src/index.ts); the app composes the widgets, the watch and the Island's fallback (FleetPublication and FleetSnapshot in AgentKit); the daemon ranks each agent (farcooler_core::feed::rank). Read by services/relay/test/fleet-composition.test.ts, apps/shared/AgentKit/Tests/AgentKitTests/FleetCompositionTests.swift and crates/core/src/feed.rs's tests.",
    "Times are seconds before `now`: `sinceS` is how long the agent has been in its status, `heardS` how long since anything said so. `rank` is what the daemon sends for that status and `sinceS`; the relay ignores it and sorts on the status and its own clock, which is what this table holds the two to.",
    "A runner's `needsYou` is the count (relay) or the length of the list (app) it sent, null when it sent none. `quiet` is a runner that stopped beating (relay) or whose link was lost (app).",
    "Expected: `order` every agent, as each side ranks them. `blocked`, `working` and `needsYou` as the card's header and the widgets count them, and `header` the number they lead with: `needsYou` when any runner counted, else `blocked`. `review` (done agents) and `shown` (the card's lines, at most four) are the relay's alone: the app's widgets count reviews by worktree, and draw every agent.",
    "No `failed` agent yet: ov-125 adds the relay's failed outcome and should add its cases here."
  ],
  "now": 1790000000000,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an empty fleet counts nothing and says no runner counted",
      "runners": [],
      "agents": [],
      "expect": {
        "order": [],
        "blocked": 0, "review": 0, "working": 0, "needsYou": null, "header": 0,
        "shown": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "blocked, then done, then working, then a status the card draws no tier for; the longest waiting first; the terminal breaks a tie",
